## International Chopin Festival

The **Chopin Festival** is the cultural highlight of the year. Since 1960, world-renowned pianists have come to Marienbad every August to perform in the town's most atmospheric venues: the Casino, the Nový Lázně and the Main Colonnade. The festival commemorates Chopin's stay in the summer of 1836 and has become one of **Europe's most prestigious piano festivals**.

Concerts, masterclasses, competitions and film screenings form a week-long programme that attracts music lovers from around the world. Tickets are in high demand — early booking recommended.

## Town Theatre (Městské divadlo)

The neoclassical Town Theatre, built in 1868, offers a year-round programme of **opera, ballet, drama and concerts**. The intimate format — the hall seats approximately 400 guests — makes every theatre visit a special experience. Guest performances by national and international ensembles complement the local programme.

## Casino (Společenský dům)

The **Casino** is one of the town's finest buildings — a Neo-Renaissance masterpiece that serves as a cultural and events centre. The magnificent ballroom hosts concerts, balls and exhibitions. The atmosphere alone is worth a visit.

## Singing Fountain

The **Zpívající fontána** in front of the Main Colonnade is Marienbad's most iconic landmark. Every odd hour (7am–7pm in season), water dances in time to music — from Dvořák and Chopin to popular melodies. The evening performances with light effects after dark are particularly impressive.

## Museums

- **Městské muzeum (Town Museum)** — The history of Marienbad from marshy valley to world-class spa resort. Historical spa equipment, photographs, guest books of famous visitors.
- **Goethe House** — Memories of the poet's stays and his love for Ulrike von Levetzow.
- **Geological Museum** — The science behind the springs and the volcanic history of the region.

## Seasonal Events

- **Spring:** Opening of the spa season, first outdoor concerts
- **Summer:** Chopin Festival, Singing Fountain, open-air concerts
- **Autumn:** Goethe Days, harvest festival, autumn concerts
- **Winter:** Advent markets, Christmas concerts, New Year's Eve gala

## Architecture

Marienbad itself is an open-air museum of architecture: **Neo-Renaissance, Neo-Baroque, Art Nouveau and Classicism** stand in harmonious coexistence. Guided architecture tours are available through the Tourist Information Centre. Highlights include: the Main Colonnade (1889), the Church of the Assumption, Hotel Nové Lázně and the Art Nouveau villas along Třebízského ulice.
